  card="Atoms of an element can combine to form a molecule of that element, for example a hydrogen molecule consists of two hydrogen atoms, and atoms of different elements combine to form a molecule of a compound, for example one hydrogen atom and one chlorine atom combine to form hydrogen chloride. A molecule is an electrically neutral entity consisting of more than one atom that is capable of independent existence and shows all the properties of that substance. Some elements such as helium exist only as atoms because their atoms are stable. Atoms with 8 electrons in the outermost shell (2 if the K shell is the outermost) are stable; if the valence shell has fewer than eight, atoms may share, gain or lose electrons to complete it, and in this process atoms of elements combine to form compounds. This generally takes place in two ways: sharing of electrons, and transfer of electrons. When atoms combine the total energy of the system becomes lower than the sum of the energies of the individual atoms, making the arrangement more stable. The force that holds atoms together is called a chemical bond.",
